{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794445406693877685,"compiled_state":{"alias":"sulfuric-zebraic-hackee","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"ce4407f3c70782525ae331ca5b5a9de950519d8216c4f168c92a6a15cf606ecc","event_uuid":"5bd1137c-b2c1-4e0c-a215-a88be27f60d2","position":{"commit_sha":"9bfa8b6dadd12c54a03bf836c65aa17e77e313ab","position":"1794445323960507042-5bd1137c-b2c1-4e0c-a215-a88be27f60d2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"86647f6b37ae47ee35d1200a6004ada22a84ea25e50aaaa3b75201cb6697315d","event_uuid":"d87e4a8a-469e-4e69-b475-f63fdae1f27f","position":{"commit_sha":"d18a3917e3da7b0009edbbfc7d951e5b68772ab8","position":"1794445406693877684-d87e4a8a-469e-4e69-b475-f63fdae1f27f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794445323960507042,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d87e4a8a-469e-4e69-b475-f63fdae1f27f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3e48-86e5-45a7-4acd"}],"description":"## Sunset ticket for the `lock maintenance.lock` mechanism marker\n\nThe fix for bug `saccharine-unwise-barnacle` makes the explicit store maintenance step (`event_commit_git.run_auto_maintenance`) remove `<common-dir>/objects/maintenance.lock` when the lock is older than 12 hours. That code is the `# mechanism-ok: lock maintenance.lock` marker in `src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py`, and this ticket is its sunset.\n\nIt exists because git never expires that lock. `builtin/gc.c` `maintenance_run_tasks` returns 0 without doing any work when it cannot take the lock, and unlike `gc.pid` it has no staleness rule.\n\n## When to act\n\nDo this when either condition holds:\n- Upstream git expires a stale maintenance lock itself, and every rebar runtime (the MCP container image and the supported local git floor) ships that version.\n- Store maintenance moves out of the post-write step, for example to a scheduled job that owns its own lock recovery.\n\n## Plan\n\nDelete `_reclaim_stale_maintenance_lock` and its call, the `_MAINTENANCE_LOCK_STALE_S` constant, the marker, and `tests/unit/test_store_maintenance_lock_reclaim.py`. Then run `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py` no longer removes `objects/maintenance.lock`, and no `mechanism-ok` marker names this ticket.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":4,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6dee-f9be-9a2f-41ae","ticket_type":"task","title":"Retire rebar's stale maintenance.lock reclaim once git expires that lock itself","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5bd1137c-b2c1-4e0c-a215-a88be27f60d2","d87e4a8a-469e-4e69-b475-f63fdae1f27f"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794445406693877685,"uuid":"f666d018-0cd1-489b-b788-9eef44ead0ef"}